title: The First Hello
id: intro-studio404
tab: The first hello
about: Six verses in turn, then the whole workshop on the chorus
arrangement: introduction
lead: vee
key: D major
bpm: 116
bass: none
breath: .25

tune hello = 0 2 4 2 1 0 1 0/.75 | I 4, IV 4
tune reply = 0 1 2 4 3 2 1 0/.75 | V 4, I 4

[vee]
vee: "I'm Neon two tubes in a box" = hello
vee: "I hum twin notes around the clocks" = reply
turnaround V 4

[scribe]
scribe: "I am Cue I read ev'ry line" = hello
scribe: "I turn my scroll so friends can shine" = reply
turnaround V 4

[clank]
clank: "I am Clank I boot up my screen" = hello
clank: "Silver tape keeps my old frame clean" = reply
turnaround V 4

[pip]
pip: "I am Watt my red switch glows bright" = hello
pip: "Plug in with me and sing tonight" = reply
turnaround V 4

[gruff]
gruff: "I am Gruff my valves hum so low" = hello
gruff: "Sit close by and share my warm glow" = reply
turnaround V 4

[tabby]
tabby: "I am Tabby stitched from old cloth" = hello
tabby: "My cracked screen purrs and keeps us warm" = reply
turnaround V 4

[chip]
chip: "I am Chip my floppy spins bright" = hello
chip: "Circuit crest gleams into the night" = reply
turnaround V 4

[zap]
zap: "I am Zap I change the channel" = hello
zap: "Every button means I'm sure" = reply
turnaround V 4

[chorus]
"We are the scraps that found a song" = hello
"At four oh four we all belong" = reply
